
══ upgrade judgement (advisory; AI judgement for an engineer to approve or deny) ══
acme v1.0.0 → v1.1.0 · environment prod
Recommendation  MODIFY-TARGET
Headline        Modify target to 1.1.3; keep the pinned mode, then upgrade; provided the flag stays unset; start test required before production.
Scope           the repository's configuration
Precondition    the flag is not set outside the repository

── target version ──
  current v1.0.0 · proposed v1.1.0 · minimum safe v1.1.2 · recommended by rule v1.1.3 · CHOSEN v1.1.3
  rule: v1.1.3 is the latest known patch on line 1.1: it removes every regression and adds no assessed advisory v1.1.2 is free of, so it is recommended (PD-3); v1.1.2 is the minimum.
  - proposed      v1.1.0     NOT SAFE. v1.1.0 is the proposed target; it introduces GHSA-r, which v1.0.0 is free of.
      still affected by: GHSA-r
  - minimum       v1.1.2     safe. 1.1.2 is the lowest known release on line 1.1 that removes every regression.
      chart acme 1.1.2
  - latest-patch  v1.1.3     safe. v1.1.3 is the latest known patch on line 1.1; checked against 2 assessed advisories of the product, it is affected by none v1.0.0 or v1.1.2 is free of.
      chart acme 1.1.3
      not assessable: GHSA-u
  ! the v1.0.0 → v1.1.3 transition has not been investigated; that investigation is required (see validation).

  rationale: the proposed target regresses security

